@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-availability-uses-booking-overlap-semantics
+type: decision-log
+title: "Availability uses booking overlap semantics"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The desk needs to determine which equipment is free for an entire requested rental period. Existing
+bookings use half-open UTC day intervals and allow adjacent bookings.
+
+## Decision
+
+Availability uses the existing overlap predicate: a piece of equipment is unavailable only when its
+booking overlaps the requested half-open interval. An optional `kind` limits the result to boards or
+sails; ids are sorted before returning.
+
+## Consequences
+
+An item remains available when a booking ends at the query start or begins at the query end. The
+availability query and booking operation apply identical period boundaries.
